   "title": "Typical point-to-point full-duplex application",
   "page": 12,
   "description": "Two ADM1490E on two twisted pairs, one pair for each direction. The left node's driver (Y, Z) feeds the right node's receiver (A, B), and the right node's driver feeds the left node's receiver. Each pair is terminated at its receiving end with RT across the two wires, plus a resistor from one wire to VCC and one from the other wire to ground. RT equals the cable's characteristic impedance. At most 32 nodes share a bus.",
